      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it is a way of resolving the issue, this is why I declared them in DEFAULT_AUTH_METHODS in a previous version of the patch.\n\nThe cause of the error is that we\u0027re in a rather new situation where some auth methods are not declared as default but already have a default driver. When running setup_authentication, the behavior is to declare a minimal option (line 1066) and add it to the conf, but then we hit a duplicate option error in oslo.config (since the default option is different). Since we hit this in a very specific context, I chose to pass the exception silently. Any other non-default auth method will be registered the usual way.\n\nI think it\u0027s better to leave the auth methods that require some specific apache configuration out of the DEFAULT_AUTH_METHODS and go this way. WDYT ?",
